Below is a brief summary of what’s going on and what we need to change, followed by two concrete `*SEARCH/REPLACE*` patches—one for Scala and one for JavaScript.

1) Scala bug (“`//` comments after a class declaration without a `{` end up being picked up as part of the class title”)

   In `src/languages/scala.js` the `CLASS` mode ends on a newline (`\n`), so

     class A  // comment
     { …

   never “closes” the class header before the comment; the comment itself is still inside the class title span. We simply remove `\n` from the end‐regex so that only an explicit `{`, `:` or similar stops the class header.

2) JS bug (“comments inside an arrow‐function parameter list are not highlighted”)

   Inside the “value” container that tries to detect arrow functions, there is a sub‐mode for arrow‐functions which only includes the `params` submode. We need to also allow line‐ and block‐comments in that submode’s `contains` so that

     f = ( /* comment */ x ) => …

   will correctly highlight `/* comment */` inside the `(`…`)`.

